+//! Bulk `DeleteObjects` — `POST /bucket?delete` (issue #509). Drives the gateway's S3
+//! wire surface with a **stock `aws-sdk-s3`** client (`delete_objects()`, which builds the
+//! signed POST + `<Delete>` XML body for real — mirrors `s3_gateway_cluster.rs`'s
+//! `sdk_client` / `s3_http_wire.rs::real_sdk_interop::sdk_client`) over the same in-process
+//! redb + fs-tempdir loopback stack `s3_object_metadata.rs` stands up.
+//!
+//! Asserted (brief success criterion): a bulk delete naming several present keys and at
+//! least one absent one answers `200` with a `<DeleteResult>` naming each requested key
+//! exactly once — `<Deleted>` for BOTH the removed and the already-absent keys (S3 delete
+//! is idempotent) — and a follow-up `GetObject` of a deleted key is `404 NoSuchKey`;
+//! `Quiet=true` omits the `<Deleted>` entries; a malformed XML body is `400 MalformedXML`;
+//! more than 1000 keys is refused; and an entity-escaped key (`&amp;` etc.) deletes the
+//! right object.
+//!
+//! RED on the wave base: `POST /bucket?delete` falls through the bucket-scoped dispatch to
+//! `400 InvalidRequest` (non-GET bucket-scoped methods) or is denylisted straight to `501`
+//! (the `delete` subresource, `crates/gateway-s3/src/lib.rs` `UNSUPPORTED_SUBRESOURCES`) —
+//! either way never a `200 <DeleteResult>` — so every assertion below fails pre-fix. GREEN
+//! once the bulk-delete route exists.
+
